 ## Author decisions
 
-None.
+- 2026-10-01: Keep the existing `apps/web` layout (`app/`, `components/<area>/`, `lib/<area>/`; no `src/`, no `features/`). TS-090/091 removed from Notion; PATTERN-001–003 are now SHOULD.
+- 2026-10-01: One shared fetcher module, `lib/api/api-fetcher.ts`; no per-endpoint hooks. NOM-4 adds `useCursorFetcher` beside `useFetcher`/`useInfiniteFetcher` (which stays page-based for `DataInfiniteTable`). TS-100 rewritten in Notion.
+- 2026-10-01: Every NOM-4 API call validates its response with a Zod `schema` passed to the fetcher; schemas live in `types/search.ts`. TS-101 rewritten in Notion.
+- 2026-10-02: Web UI and fetcher tests answer HTTP with MSW (`msw` 2.15.0, dev only; 2.x to match Vitest 2's peer) via the opt-in helper `apps/web/tests/msw.ts`, so the real fetcher runs (TS-141, TEST-003). Existing tests are migrated in a separate ticket. Server route tests keep mocking Prisma; mobile keeps stubbing `fetch` through its real `lib/api.ts` client.
+- 2026-10-02: Cache keys come from the existing `generateQueryKey` in `api-fetcher.ts`, extended with the signed-in viewer (or anonymous); logout/block resets use the same function. TS-024 rewritten in Notion.
+- 2026-10-02: Mobile validates the new `searchPage` response with Zod (`zod` 4.4.3 added to `apps/mobile`, the web's version). Other mobile calls gain schemas when touched.
+- 2026-10-02 (replaces R6): Mobile Explore keeps the sort in its route params (`?sort=`), like `course`, so it is restored and linkable (TS-025). Spec F8 updated.
 
