 ### Mobile
-- `(tabs)/explore.tsx` uses `useInfiniteQuery` and `onEndReached` for opt-in cursor pages; pull-to-refresh reloads page one for the current query, filters and sort. Sort chips are included in both the request and query identity. Changing a chip, query or filter abandons old pages and cursors; late old responses cannot append. Prevent duplicate end-reached requests; retain visible rows and offer retry on a later-page failure, distinguish first-page failure from an empty result, and show exhaustion only after a successful terminal page. Chip selection lives in component state only: it resets to the default sort (`newest` for empty `q`, `relevance` otherwise) whenever the screen remounts, and deep links do not set it. *Decision 2026-09-30 (R6): reset on remount, no deep-link sort in this release.*
